//! The `box-decoration-break` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property
//! specifies how an element's
//! [fragments](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Fragmentation) should be
//! rendered when broken across multiple lines, columns, or pages.
//!
//! Initial: slice. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - clone: Each box fragment is rendered independently with the specified border, padding, and
//! margin wrapping each fragment. The , , and are applied to each fragment independently. The
//! background is also drawn independently for each fragment, which means that a background image
//! with may nevertheless repeat multiple times.
//! - slice: The element is initially rendered as if its box were not fragmented, after which the
//! rendering for this hypothetical box is sliced into pieces for each line/column/page. Note that
//! the hypothetical box can be different for each fragment since it uses its own height if the break
//! occurs in the inline direction, and its own width if the break occurs in the block direction. See
//! the CSS specification for details.
//!
//! Grammar: slice | clone
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-break-4/#propdef-box-decoration-break
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/box-decoration-break
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

